---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { absolute, canonical, imageAttrs, mediumArticles, shortMonthYear } from '../lib/site';

const articles = mediumArticles();
const rank = (i: number) => String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0');

// The page's own schema.org graph, assembled from the same data the list uses.
const graph = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Book',
      '@id': `${canonical('/books/')}#dreaming-of-a-hopeful-death`,
      name: 'Dreaming of a Hopeful Death',
      author: {
        '@type': 'Person',
        name: 'A. S. Mori',
        url: 'https://www.amazon.com/author/a.s.mori'
      },
      datePublished: '2023-01-30',
      inLanguage: 'en',
      bookFormat: 'https://schema.org/EBook',
      url: 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BT4ZYKTF',
      image: absolute('assets/images/books/Dreaming of a Hopeful Death/Front Cover.jpg'),
      description:
        'An experimental, introspective science fiction novel about humanity fused into a single being and forced to wander the universe until its heat death.',
      sameAs: [
        'https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/104086124-dreaming-of-a-hopeful-death',
        'https://a-s-mori.itch.io/dreaming-of-a-hopeful-death'
      ]
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ItemList',
      '@id': `${canonical('/books/')}#most-read-essays`,
      name: 'Most-Read Essays',
      description:
        'The five articles by Avinash Saravanan that found the widest audience on Medium, by lifetime views.',
      numberOfItems: articles.length,
      itemListOrder: 'https://schema.org/ItemListOrderDescending',
      itemListElement: articles.map((article, i) => ({
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: i + 1,
        item: {
          '@type': 'CreativeWork',
          name: article.title,
          url: article.url,
          datePublished: article.date,
          image: absolute(article.image),
          author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Avinash Saravanan' }
        }
      }))
    }
  ]
};
---

<Base
  title="Books"
  description="Books published by Avinash Saravanan under the pen name A. S. Mori."
  image="/assets/images/books/books-top.jpg"
  styleSheet="/assets/css/pages/books.css"
>
<div class="page-top">
    <span class="hero-floor" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
    <div class="books-preamble">
        <h1 class="text-center"><span>Books</span></h1>
    </div>
    <div class="books-explanation">
        <p>Books I have published under my penname A. S. Mori</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section id="Dreaming of a Hopeful Death" class="book-section">
    <div class="book-layout">
        <div class="book-cover-column">
            <a class="book-cover-link" target="_blank" href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BT4ZYKTF">
                <img class="cover" src="/assets/images/books/Dreaming%20of%20a%20Hopeful%20Death/Front%20Cover.jpg" width="1604" height="2560" alt="Dreaming of a Hopeful Death cover" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
            </a>
            <div class="book-meta">
                <p><a target="_blank" href="https://www.amazon.com/author/a.s.mori">A. S. Mori</a>: Jan 30, 2023</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="book-text-column">
            <a class="book-title" target="_blank" href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BT4ZYKTF">
                <h2 class="heading">Dreaming of a Hopeful Death</h2>
            </a>
            <div class="book-explanation">
                <p>Our civilization, despite all its achievements, is hopelessly unaware of the dangers that lurk beyond our senses and beyond our third dimension.
                    It is only when it is too late that we realize how little we know and how powerless we are.
                    In the near future, the human race is transformed into one being with the memories of billions and forced to wander the universe endlessly till the end where nothing is left.
                    As centuries turn into trillions of years, the sanity of Humanity is brought to the brink as it questions what it sees out there in the vacuum of space and looks back upon the past it barely remembers in a desperate attempt to secure a mental foothold that somewhat resembles what it once experienced when it was billions of people walking the earth.
                </p>
                <p>Dreaming of a Hopeful Death is an experimental, introspective, philosophical and science fiction journey through the universe which tries to answer the question of what would happen if the entirety of the human race had its free will taken away and was forced on an unending trip through space until the heat death of the universe.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="book-personal">
                <p>This is my debut novel under the penname A. S. Mori and is hopefully the first of many.
                    It is available under ebook format, paperback, and hardcover.
                    I also adapted it as a visual novel and made it available for free on <a href="https://a-s-mori.itch.io/dreaming-of-a-hopeful-death" target="_blank">Itch.io</a>.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="book-links">
                <a target="_blank" href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BT4ZYKTF">Amazon</a>
                <a target="_blank" href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/104086124-dreaming-of-a-hopeful-death">Goodreads</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
<hr>
<section id="substack" class="substack-section">
    <div class="substack-intro">
        <h2 class="heading">Substack Newsletter</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="substack-frame">
        <iframe class="substack" src="https://asmori.substack.com/embed" height="320" title="Substack Newsletter" frameborder="0" scrolling="no"></iframe>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="writing" class="writing-section">
    <div class="writing-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Elsewhere</p>
        <h2 class="heading">Most-Read Essays</h2>
        <p class="writing-note">The five pieces that found the widest audience on Medium, by lifetime views.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="writing-list">
        {articles.map((article, i) => (
        <li class="writing-item">
            <a class="writing-link" href={article.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <span class="writing-rank" aria-hidden="true">{rank(i)}</span>
                <span class="writing-thumb">
                    <img src={`/${article.image}`} {...imageAttrs(`/${article.image}`)} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                </span>
                <span class="writing-body">
                    <span class="writing-title">{article.title}</span>
                    {article.blurb && <span class="writing-blurb">{article.blurb}</span>}
                    <span class="writing-meta">
                        <time datetime={article.date}>{shortMonthYear(article.date)}</time>
                        {article.views && <span class="writing-views">{article.views} views</span>}
                    </span>
                </span>
                <span class="writing-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
        </li>
        ))}
    </ol>
    <a class="writing-more" href="https://medium.com/@asarav" target="_blank" rel="noopener">All articles on Medium <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(graph)} />
</Base>
